WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.000
It has never played before, so it moves at random.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.000
When a game ends, what happened is saved to a shared memory.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.000
The same level and starting position, after 431,173 decisions.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Every move now comes from what earlier games remembered.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.000
128 games play at once and write to the same memory.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.000
The curve follows eight games that always choose the best-scoring move.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Venn embeds each screen with EmbeddingGemma 2 and looks up similar moments.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.500
For each move, it averages how those moments turned out.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:41.000
At quarter speed: it returns the move with the best record, and the game plays it.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.000
The game client makes one call for a batch of 128 screens.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.000
The game owns the memory store, and Venn reads it through an adapter.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Another recorded round with the same memory.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.000
This round finishes with 6 kills.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.000
One more call compiles the memory into a small head.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.000
The head has 49,000 parameters and fits in 200 kilobytes.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.500
Same level, with the memory switched off.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.000
The head alone picks every move.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:26.000
This round finishes with 13 kills.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:32.000
The whole loop, including the game itself, runs on one GPU.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Across 250 scored games, the head averaged 8.4 kills per game.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.000
The memory it learned from averaged 6.2.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.000
A memory of raw pixels averaged 4.9, and random moves averaged 1.3.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.000
The embedding model is pretrained and frozen.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.000
The head is the only trained part.
